     1	/**
     2	 * shellCommands.ts — the actions the /next command palette offers.
     3	 *
     4	 * Registration is pure bookkeeping: it stores functions in the palette's
     5	 * registry and calls none of them, so it is safe at component init and must
     6	 * never be put in an `$effect`. Each action is a plain sentence a user can read
     7	 * without knowing how the shell is built.
     8	 *
     9	 * The palette seeds "Reset layout", "Look for agent sessions" and "Open
    10	 * settings" itself from the callbacks the page passes it; everything here is
    11	 * the panels' own actions.
