    90	// ── which folder to ask ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    91	
    92	/**
    93	 * The top of the repository a folder belongs to, or `null` when nothing can
    94	 * work it out.
    95	 *
    96	 * WHY THIS MATTERS. `git show <sha> -- <path>` matches the path against the
    97	 * folder git is run in, not against the top of the repository. Ask from a
    98	 * subfolder with a repository-relative path and git matches nothing, prints
    99	 * nothing, and reports success — a blank diff that reads exactly like "this
   100	 * file did not change". The panel is pointed at whatever folder a session is
   101	 * working in, and that is often a subfolder, so the top has to be worked out
   102	 * rather than assumed.
