     1	/**
     2	 * gitCommitFilesService.ts — the git calls behind an open commit in the graph.
     3	 *
     4	 * The same rules `gitService.ts` is built on, for the same reasons:
     5	 *
     6	 *  - **Nothing loads at import, and nothing reacts.** No `$effect`. A commit's
     7	 *    file list is read when somebody opens that commit, and never otherwise.
     8	 *  - **Every question goes to the top of the repository.** `git show <sha> --
     9	 *    <path>` matches the path against the folder git is run in, so asking from
    10	 *    a subfolder matches nothing and reports success — a blank answer that
    11	 *    reads as "this file did not change". The panel is often pointed at a
    12	 *    session's working folder, which is frequently NOT the top, so the top is
    13	 *    worked out once per repository and every call uses it.
    14	 *  - **A slow answer never overwrites a newer one.** Same monotonic request id
    15	 *    as the rest of the panel.
    16	 *  - **No stand-in data.** When neither the desktop app nor the dev server can
    17	 *    answer, the row says so in one sentence.
    18	 *
    19	 * The diff itself is shown by the existing `GitDiffView`, which reads
    20	 * `gitPanel`. So picking a file inside a commit writes into that same state —
    21	 * after letting go of whatever working-copy diff was on screen, so the two
    22	 * cannot race each other into the view.
    23	 */
