   168	
   169	/**
   170	 * Start a saved run configuration: ask the page for a session running its
   171	 * command, tag that session as this configuration's, then read the ports again.
   172	 *
   173	 * The port read happens straight away and will usually still show "started, no
   174	 * port yet" — a dev server takes a second or two to bind. That is deliberate:
   175	 * the alternative is a timer, and this lane does not poll. The refresh button
   176	 * (and the row's own click) is how the user asks again.
   177	 *
   178	 * The environment variables are folded into the command line HERE rather than
   179	 * anywhere further in, so nothing downstream has to learn about them: the page
   180	 * gets one command line and spawns it exactly as it always has, and the honest
   181	 * exit code that comes back still belongs to the command the user asked for.
   182	 */
